# Flutter Performance and Accessibility

- Avoid unnecessary widget rebuilds and expensive work during `build()`.
- Paginate large historical lists.
- Avoid loading large media files into memory unnecessarily.
- Compress/resize evidence photos according to documented quality/storage requirements before upload when safe.
- Schedule background synchronization carefully to protect battery and data usage.
- Avoid frequent GPS sampling unless operationally required.
- Use accessible labels, touch targets, contrast, semantics, and scalable text.
- Measure before introducing complex performance optimizations.
